#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064154 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064037 :question/id #uuid "750e7350-1434-56ef-80d8-7cf531108f96" :question/math-academy-id "e-273" :question/problem "On a particular day, the rate $E$ at which tourists enter a small country can be modeled as $E(t) = 50\\cdot 3^{0.2t}$ tourists per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, after midnight. The rate at which tourists leave the country can be modeled as $L(t)=100\\cdot 2^{0.2t}$ tourists per hour, where $t$ is also the time in hours after midnight.\n\nWhat is the rate of change in the number of tourists in the country at $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}?$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of the number of tourists in the country at time $t$ is equal to the entry rate minus the exit rate at time $t,$ that is, \n\n$$\nE(t)-L(t).\n$$\n\nSince $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}$ is ten hours after midnight, we have $t=10.$ Substituting $t=10,$ the rate of change in the number of tourists in the country at $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E(10)-L(10) & =50\\cdot {3}^{0.2(10)}-100\\cdot {2}^{0.2(10)} \\\\  & =450-400 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the number of tourists in the country at $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}$ is $50$ tourists per hour."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7df31c9-b27a-5ce2-93c8-178ba96da000" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064839 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0471e9db-ae74-5721-881f-6766ec471aab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$55$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063092} {:answer/id #uuid "0cb451c9-624d-5aea-a847-0a716186f298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063093} {:answer/id #uuid "19b1cbfa-5dc1-50c7-b795-45e8078bcfc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063094} {:answer/id #uuid "1b66f55e-690d-507d-9f15-da5db4e9d4d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$77$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063095} {:answer/id #uuid "20cf6a46-231f-5311-8a1f-d91f99078953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$66$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cb451c9-624d-5aea-a847-0a716186f298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063093} :answer-field/id #uuid "68d15ded-f5ea-533d-bc58-1b30eba5bad8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063091}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7cc5ee70-2b10-5325-a2dc-cd7c11e6d8be" :question/math-academy-id "q-48935" :question/problem "The birth rate of crocodiles in a river is modeled by $B(t)=6\\cdot {e}^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t)=4\\cdot {e}^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, where $t$ represents the number of years since the year $2000.$  \n\nWhat was the rate of change of the crocodile population in $2012?$ Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change in the crocodile population $t$ years since $2000$ is equal to the birth rate minus the death rate, that is\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nSince $2012$ is $12$ years after $2000$, we have $t=12.$ Substituting $t=12,$ the rate of change of the crocodile population in the river  in $2012$ was\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(12)-D(12) & =6\\cdot {e}^{0.25(12)}-4\\cdot {e}^{0.25(12)} \\\\  & =6{e}^{3}-4{e}^{3} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3} \\\\  & ≈40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of the crocodile population in the river in $2012$ is approximately $40$ crocodiles per year."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82402f4c-fc78-5115-abbb-8ad3dc43491f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063098} {:answer/id #uuid "cc715b82-ec3a-5165-93b6-be32e1b392a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1.4$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063099} {:answer/id #uuid "fab10240-8482-561c-8059-251f3e1c7340" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ liter per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063100} {:answer/id #uuid "47d9e4ac-1056-5034-b06d-e6db26008fa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063101} {:answer/id #uuid "6c4a5028-9eb2-5a86-a7ba-fc7fb96b071f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1.5$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063102}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e37c85c4-0030-5b58-beda-4e374bfaab62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063097}] :question/id #uuid "d91740bb-0717-56e4-8960-7951b9ef1956" :question/math-academy-id "q-48936" :question/problem "The rate $F$ at which a swimming pool is being filled can be modeled as $F(t) = t^{2} - t$ liters per minute, where $t$ is the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled. The rate at which water is leaking from the pool can be modeled as $L(t) = \\frac{1}{4}t^{2}$ liters per minute, where $t$ is also the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled.\n\nWhat is the rate of change of the volume of water in the pool $2$ minutes after the pool began to be filled?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233148 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04af5409-c23e-5a9b-9822-6f64b5d41018" :question/math-academy-id "q-112382" :question/problem "After taking a pill containing $300$ milligrams of a particular drug, the quantity of the drug in a patient's body decreases at a rate of $c(t)=300\\cdot {2}^{-0.7t}$ milligrams per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the patient consumed the pill. What will be the rate of decrease after $5$ hours? Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to determine the rate of decrease in the quantity of the drug in the patient's body after $5$ hours, we have $t=5.$\n\nThus, the rate of decrease in the quantity of the drug after $5$ hours will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c(5) & =300\\cdot {2}^{-0.7(5)} \\\\  & =300\\cdot {2}^{-3.5} \\\\  & \\approx 27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of decrease will be $27$ milligrams per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b018299-7007-54eb-bc89-99c9efa7a6a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b018299-7007-54eb-bc89-99c9efa7a6a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232200} :answer-field/id #uuid "60e7eb70-1c1f-5c79-88b8-72f4909c2ea9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232199}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d565b38-f76f-5424-8185-fe15e9499b1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142994" :question/problem "What was the exact rate of change of the stock's value at week $9?$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ thousand dollars per week." :question/worked-solution "The function ${h}^{'}(x)$ models the rate of change of the value of the stock, applicable in the domain of $h(x).$\n\nThus, the rate of change of the value of the stock at $x=9$ weeks is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{'}(9) & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the stock price was $\\frac{1}{9}$ thousand dollars per week."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234095 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e0f698f-6d3a-555d-aa86-2a4465688985" :question/math-academy-id "q-48608" :question/problem "The birth rate of a krill population is modeled by $B(t)=5\\cdot {2}^{0.7t}$ thousands of tons per year, where $t$ is the time, in years, since $1998.$ What was the birth rate, in thousands of tons per year, for the krill in $2008?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $B(t)$ models the birth rate for the krill, in thousands of tons, $t$ years since $1998.$ Since we want the birth rate in $2008$, then $t=10$ years.\n\nThus, the birth rate for the krill in $2008$ was\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(10) & =5\\cdot {2}^{0.7(10)} \\\\  & =5\\cdot {2}^{7} \\\\  & =640.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the birth rate for the krill in $2008$ was $640$ thousand tons per year."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae60046d-e068-5985-a664-cad5d031ad4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae60046d-e068-5985-a664-cad5d031ad4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234812} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9203a5f-745f-5240-bf02-625bcda44d5b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235251}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e0e7cbce-5689-5b4d-bba5-cc1bd41aa26a" :question/math-academy-id "q-167562" :question/problem "What was the exact rate of change of the stock's value at week $4?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,$ thousand dollars per week." :question/worked-solution "The function ${g}^{′}(x)$ models the rate of change of the value of the stock, applicable in the domain of $g(x).$\n\nThus, the rate of change of the value of the stock at $x=4$ weeks is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the stock price was $\\frac{1}{2}$ thousand dollars per week."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f69ffc3-967d-568e-b3f6-17f98cabb1f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.899$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244455} {:answer/id #uuid "623719cf-e4fc-50c5-af6b-82c9236bba68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.736$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245173} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8c808d-a723-5a23-99d4-1fb6cf45cc5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.311$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245689} {:answer/id #uuid "defc4fee-1f26-5c5d-84cf-ab714d860a2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.346$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246291} {:answer/id #uuid "e54a6975-4261-5825-a3df-b1afbd880b9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.566$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "623719cf-e4fc-50c5-af6b-82c9236bba68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.736$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245173} :answer-field/id #uuid "6afb29aa-f1d1-5f09-9077-99008241eb9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246734}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c8932d66-35b8-594b-9a87-80583a008ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-112381" :question/problem "The decay rate $M$ of muons in a beam traveling at high speed can be modeled by the function $M(t)=2\\cdot {e}^{-2t},$ where $t$ is the time, in microseconds, since observations started. What will be the decay rate of the muons after $0.5$ microseconds? Round your answer to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The function $M(t)$ models the decay rate for the particles $t$ microseconds since observations started.\n\nThus, the decay rate of the muons after $0.5$ microseconds is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(0.5) & =2\\cdot {e}^{-2(0.5)} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {e}^{-1} \\\\  & ≈0.736.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the decay rate of the particles is $0.736$ muons per microsecond."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04171382-cbfa-5f10-92fb-22e5c7a6e6de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244346} {:answer/id #uuid "284bf059-1884-5e2d-a5c3-731890221cc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244669} {:answer/id #uuid "51d5b6bd-e195-5c6e-bf88-1a79c021dc21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245038} {:answer/id #uuid "6d228c5d-7d6a-5f80-841c-f0172b125cc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245278} {:answer/id #uuid "7452c71d-92bf-59ad-847f-f7ba52f5ece7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04171382-cbfa-5f10-92fb-22e5c7a6e6de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244346} :answer-field/id #uuid "4de83a2e-a171-5c7c-a155-600eb37ea0f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246677}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "524d3949-c8de-5ba0-b1ba-ea4e8e41e832" :question/math-academy-id "q-112383" :question/problem "After charging the battery of a PC, the percentage of charge decreases at a rate of $c(t)=100\\cdot {5}^{-0.2t}$ percent per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the battery had completed its charge. What will be the rate of decrease after $5$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "Since we want to determine the rate of decrease in the amount of charge after $5$ hours, we have $t=5.$\n\nThus, the rate of decrease of the amount of charge after $5$ hours will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c(5) & =100\\cdot {5}^{-0.2(5)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {5}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{100}{5} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of decrease will be $20$ percent per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f1c6b98-25f8-5e4b-b169-c98a156923ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$162$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245016} {:answer/id #uuid "779d5d52-77eb-5021-9fdb-6949a0551730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$140$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245373} {:answer/id #uuid "811be8e1-8e6b-5190-8d78-5e4b9cd0b31b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$125$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245455} {:answer/id #uuid "c45a009c-113a-5c51-b8a5-aee9dd3c26fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$100$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246059} {:answer/id #uuid "e07a4990-5522-544f-8f86-dacc8fa566a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$120$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e07a4990-5522-544f-8f86-dacc8fa566a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$120$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246309} :answer-field/id #uuid "78d8582c-8f74-5c8e-a7a1-5a0e9065a5b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246756}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b547e5e1-1e78-5d71-9ff5-a1728add6182" :question/math-academy-id "q-112507" :question/problem "The rate $O$ of the orders a car factory receives can be modeled as $O(t)=100t{e}^{-0.1t}$ cars per day. The rate at which cars are completed can be modeled as $C(t)=50+10sin⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{7}t)$ cars per day. In both cases, $t$ is the time, in days, since the launch of the new model. \n\nWhat is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction $28$ days after the model's launch? Assume that an ordered car goes into construction as soon as the factory receives its order. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of the number of cars under construction at time $t$ is equal to the order rate minus the completion rate, that is,\n\n$$\nO(t)-C(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $t=28,$ the rate of change in the number of cars under construction after $28$ days is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(t)-C(t) & =100(28){e}^{-0.1(28)}-(50+10sin⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{7}(28))) \\\\  & =100(28){e}^{-2.8}-50-10sin⁡(8\\pi ) \\\\  & =100(28){e}^{-2.8}-50 \\\\  & ≈120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the number of cars in construction after $28$ days is $120$ cars per day."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329934 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0400157b-c1a8-53a6-8dcd-8bf81b54d097" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$900$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326977} {:answer/id #uuid "35810fd7-3042-5428-8e3d-5d1db0348860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$800$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327400} {:answer/id #uuid "aba393d2-bfb8-5de2-8e57-d8c30468307a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$700$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328420} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f5cc60-bdc1-5422-b8c8-352e070c8ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$600$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328901} {:answer/id #uuid "ea12e4e8-1b1a-576e-8cc0-7f6378f95ca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$100\\cdot {2}^{6}$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35810fd7-3042-5428-8e3d-5d1db0348860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$800$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327400} :answer-field/id #uuid "88a2805a-ae37-515d-a7b8-d5098613d13b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329413}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46629e3f-8b91-52e2-8f67-4405ebbe6de1" :question/math-academy-id "q-48902" :question/problem "The growth rate, $G(t)$, of the number of bacteria in a culture can be modeled by the function $G(t)=100\\cdot {2}^{0.5t}$, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since a sample of bacteria was placed in a Petri dish.  What will be the growth rate of the bacteria after $6$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "The function $G(t)$ models the growth rate for the bacteria $t$ hours since the sample was put in the Petri dish.\n\nThus, the growth rate of the bacteria culture after $6$ hours is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G(6) & =100\\cdot {2}^{0.5(6)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & =100\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =800.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the growth rate of the bacteria is $800$ bacteria per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d986347-5304-5bf8-9489-b5458173cd49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-94$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327049} {:answer/id #uuid "38a1f85b-0932-59c9-8d00-d2afb106da3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-200$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327430} {:answer/id #uuid "5acea6b6-3caf-5eff-af39-aa31ffcec36a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-220$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327729} {:answer/id #uuid "d9489eab-ebee-5d5c-a32b-d59ea30a9b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$420$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328833} {:answer/id #uuid "e22a41b0-6c91-593e-ac0d-e8429be02811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$240$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38a1f85b-0932-59c9-8d00-d2afb106da3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-200$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327430} :answer-field/id #uuid "eabd25e6-300b-5d8d-ae1c-f832bb8ce89c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329593}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f24a112-83bc-5dfc-b8eb-4133c86e6e85" :question/math-academy-id "q-48914" :question/problem "The birth rate of a herd of elephants in a region in Africa is modeled by the function  $B(t)=500\\cdot {2}^{0.125t}$ while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t)=400\\cdot {3}^{0.125t}.$ In both cases, $t$ represents the number of years since $1990.$  \n\nWhat was the rate of change of the elephant population in that region in $1998?$" :question/worked-solution "The  rate of change in the number of elephants  $t$ years since $1990$ is equal to the difference between the two given rates, that is\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nAs $1998$ is $8$ years after $1990$, we have $t=8.$  Hence, the  rate of change in the elephant population in that region in $1998$ was \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(8)-D(8) & =500\\cdot {2}^{0.125(8)}-400\\cdot {3}^{0.125(8)} \\\\  & =500\\cdot 2-400\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-200.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the elephant population was $-200$ elephants per year."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dbec869-25ce-5f09-bec0-1aa8f0c5fc8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$216$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517329} {:answer/id #uuid "51c48530-c821-53d2-8682-e23e9308cc96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$248$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517334} {:answer/id #uuid "b0854dc4-f4cb-5adf-93b0-a9de2132efc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-16$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517355} {:answer/id #uuid "de87630c-5e9f-5b64-8432-c235e63365fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$232$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517372} {:answer/id #uuid "f60db18e-606e-507e-a70a-222aab527053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-216$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dbec869-25ce-5f09-bec0-1aa8f0c5fc8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$216$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517329} :answer-field/id #uuid "d55f1a11-95b1-5a99-93e1-ed8950cd0df2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517370}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4064584b-a92b-5c2b-aee4-39b559d5a1a6" :question/problem "The rate $F$ at which a swimming pool is being filled can be modeled as $F(t) = 4t^{2} - 3t$ liters per minute, where $t$ is the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled. The rate at which water is leaking from the pool can be modeled as $L(t) = \\frac{1}{4}t^{2}$ liters per minute, where $t$ is also the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled.\n\nWhat is the rate of change of the volume of water in the pool $8$ minutes after the pool began to be filled?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of the volume of water is the filling rate minus the leaking rate.\n\n$$\nF(t)-L(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $t=8$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8)-L(8) & =4(8)^{2}-3(8)-\\frac{1}{4}(8)^{2} \\\\  & =232-16 \\\\  & =216.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $216$ liters per minute."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049a0fe5-6a20-5d0a-ade6-b497853f1f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517321} {:answer/id #uuid "2e530fff-ce9c-5970-b878-96dbbaeec603" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-8$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517330} {:answer/id #uuid "89248699-5551-52fc-9603-22d4e2f2008e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517346} {:answer/id #uuid "9759bafc-fb74-5017-91e8-ab74ae726c77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517349} {:answer/id #uuid "f373a41d-03e8-5f52-b12e-d904b52de946" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89248699-5551-52fc-9603-22d4e2f2008e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517346} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f111bb-5884-576a-a701-a9d50261c695" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517324}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43cee7e4-6ff9-5eeb-9102-bb7cf335c204" :question/problem "The birth rate of crocodiles in a river is modeled by $B(t) = 4 \\cdot e^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t) = 1 \\cdot e^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, where $t$ represents the number of years since the year $2000$.\n\nWhat was the rate of change of the crocodile population in $2004$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of the crocodile population is the birth rate minus the death rate.\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nSince $2004$ is $4$ years after $2000$, substitute $t=4$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(4)-D(4) & =4\\cdot e^{0.25(4)}-1\\cdot e^{0.25(4)} \\\\  & =3\\cdot e^{1} \\\\  & \\approx 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $8$ crocodiles per year."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78aef08d-3e98-50f3-b784-97841b4c299f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78aef08d-3e98-50f3-b784-97841b4c299f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517342} :answer-field/id #uuid "aef7959b-ba6c-5639-93da-84cf1b9feb78" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517353}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "631f3d25-1539-5b45-a5e3-359eb72f3729" :question/problem "The supplied rate function is $h'(x)=\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{x}}$ thousand dollars per week, for $x>0$.\n\nWhat was the exact rate of change of the stock's value at week $144?$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ thousand dollars per week." :question/worked-solution "The function ${h}^{'}(x)$ models the rate of change of the value of the stock, applicable in the domain of $h(x).$\n\nThus, the rate of change of the value of the stock at $x=144$ weeks is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{'}(144) & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{60}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the stock price was $\\frac{1}{60}$ thousand dollars per week."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ada36c-1091-5f42-8c63-eccc8b641f55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$255$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517327} {:answer/id #uuid "b937214f-6d30-5777-98d4-63d7c6dc1a65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-105$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517358} {:answer/id #uuid "ba2e00ae-4e6a-5d71-aef7-bdb151691a73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-75$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517359} {:answer/id #uuid "cc796484-ad70-51d7-bb01-5b8342bff754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$180$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517363} {:answer/id #uuid "d16bf7d6-ca47-5047-90d1-e323cc45a658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$105$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d16bf7d6-ca47-5047-90d1-e323cc45a658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$105$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517367} :answer-field/id #uuid "60454d3c-fec5-59e1-9526-d25e77d4da41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517339}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7f4724c3-2921-55f4-a281-340d20927d04" :question/problem "A factory begins work at $8\\text{:}00$ am. Its order rate is $O(t)=140t e^{-0.2t}$ cars per hour and its completion rate is $C(t)=90+15\\sin(2\\pi t/14)$ cars per hour, where $t$ is hours after work begins. What is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction at the 24-hour time $18\\text{:}30$? Orders enter construction immediately. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change is the order rate minus the completion rate. The elapsed time is $t=(1110-480)/60=10.5$ hours.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(10.5)-C(10.5) & =140(10.5){e}^{-0.2(10.5)}-(90+15\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{14}(10.5))) \\\\  & =140(10.5){e}^{-2.1}-90-15\\sin(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}) \\\\  & =140(10.5){e}^{-2.1}-75 \\\\  & \\approx 105.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $105$ cars per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b221c18-6d59-5ed7-9a36-5ef2cdd6198b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$228$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517325} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea5bf78-0a77-58d1-9e2a-bacef9819834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-228$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517326} {:answer/id #uuid "5baff62d-cf1c-57ec-b9d7-d7a353611316" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$288$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517336} {:answer/id #uuid "9b301213-2943-5d08-a28e-082e30a5e73f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$348$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517351} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d8817e-e114-506e-a9b2-a1055123a32f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-60$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b221c18-6d59-5ed7-9a36-5ef2cdd6198b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$228$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517325} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf15e5a0-9fea-5686-9f0a-1969e5135c52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517364}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8e5ec36a-ecef-5d7c-8e17-1882b5fa8983" :question/problem "A factory begins work at $8\\text{:}00$ am. Its order rate is $O(t)=190t e^{-0.2t}$ cars per hour and its completion rate is $C(t)=50+10\\sin(2\\pi t/10)$ cars per hour, where $t$ is hours after work begins. What is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction at the 24-hour time $10\\text{:}30$? Orders enter construction immediately. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change is the order rate minus the completion rate. The elapsed time is $t=(630-480)/60=2.5$ hours.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(2.5)-C(2.5) & =190(2.5){e}^{-0.2(2.5)}-(50+10\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{10}(2.5))) \\\\  & =190(2.5){e}^{-0.5}-50-10\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\\\  & =190(2.5){e}^{-0.5}-60 \\\\  & \\approx 228.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $228$ cars per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5352939e-cae2-5159-bff4-104d22d61c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{2}{25}$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517335} {:answer/id #uuid "78f292e0-a2c7-5fcd-8ee3-576f77b454aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1000$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517343} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f9650f-e3d4-52e1-8604-95b13a333df9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{8}{25}$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517361} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a55db6-62c2-5bd7-ba6f-3238abbd84a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$100$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517368} {:answer/id #uuid "f26ac375-519e-5368-9853-c2be81821dcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{4}{25}$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f26ac375-519e-5368-9853-c2be81821dcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{4}{25}$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517375} :answer-field/id #uuid "cac29cb1-6d21-5053-bb45-5161878e9c39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517362}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a5c334a0-b9d7-58f1-b30e-102327fa70dc" :question/problem "After charging the battery of a PC, the percentage of charge decreases at a rate of $c(t)=100\\cdot {5}^{-0.4t}$ percent per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the battery had completed its charge. What will be the rate of decrease after $10$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "Since we want to determine the rate of decrease in the amount of charge after $10$ hours, we have $t=10.$\n\nThus, the rate of decrease of the amount of charge after $10$ hours will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c(10) & =100\\cdot {5}^{-0.4(10)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {5}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{100}{625} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of decrease will be $\\frac{4}{25}$ percent per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b6c992b-a9bf-50ec-a63b-953cb1055324" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-121$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517328} {:answer/id #uuid "48c1409d-fc69-54ea-b9a0-2713986d307a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-35$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517333} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb55a74-3f47-50c3-a675-afc6dec9b4f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$121$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517337} {:answer/id #uuid "b03e3130-ebeb-56a0-a735-21aa477c71ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$156$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517354} {:answer/id #uuid "de1c0611-7856-5339-b7b2-d83aedf32026" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$191$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bb55a74-3f47-50c3-a675-afc6dec9b4f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$121$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517337} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a42ed69-259b-5d9d-b5a0-92f539029c30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517350}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bd6eb95d-7375-5343-986b-68f30ad5b2d2" :question/problem "A factory begins work at $8\\text{:}00$ am. Its order rate is $O(t)=90t e^{-0.2t}$ cars per hour and its completion rate is $C(t)=20+15\\sin(2\\pi t/14)$ cars per hour, where $t$ is hours after work begins. What is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction at the 24-hour time $11\\text{:}30$? Orders enter construction immediately. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change is the order rate minus the completion rate. The elapsed time is $t=(690-480)/60=3.5$ hours.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(3.5)-C(3.5) & =90(3.5){e}^{-0.2(3.5)}-(20+15\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{14}(3.5))) \\\\  & =90(3.5){e}^{-0.7}-20-15\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\\\  & =90(3.5){e}^{-0.7}-35 \\\\  & \\approx 121.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $121$ cars per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517369 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f23811-b1ee-5151-b6b6-f608a52a57d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$76$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517323} {:answer/id #uuid "87ffd388-fbdd-5be1-b220-e00d63314682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-100$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517345} {:answer/id #uuid "90fa38bd-a1a3-5389-bd58-781b51e91810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-76$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517348} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7e8946-b8bd-5c22-9ef3-b4fcc20d9ffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$24$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517365} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9bf1a9-9ed3-510e-8652-4bea14db43c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$124$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90fa38bd-a1a3-5389-bd58-781b51e91810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-76$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517348} :answer-field/id #uuid "d104f5d3-66ed-5d0f-978b-7632a7a40047" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517366}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d1c8cfbb-47f4-5fb3-a9b0-9087d81918f8" :question/problem "A factory begins work at $8\\text{:}00$ am. Its order rate is $O(t)=50t e^{-0.1t}$ cars per hour and its completion rate is $C(t)=80+20\\sin(2\\pi t/2)$ cars per hour, where $t$ is hours after work begins. What is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction at the 24-hour time $8\\text{:}30$? Orders enter construction immediately. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change is the order rate minus the completion rate. The elapsed time is $t=(510-480)/60=0.5$ hours.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(0.5)-C(0.5) & =50(0.5){e}^{-0.1(0.5)}-(80+20\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{2}(0.5))) \\\\  & =50(0.5){e}^{-0.05}-80-20\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\\\  & =50(0.5){e}^{-0.05}-100 \\\\  & \\approx -76.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $-76$ cars per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517376 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088dec50-c3c6-50e5-9b69-0e7ce15be0f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-60$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517322} {:answer/id #uuid "6de37857-a139-5858-9e56-fc09b996a51d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$129$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517341} {:answer/id #uuid "b20f23c0-8c87-5d2b-ba53-496addf07a38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$69$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517356} {:answer/id #uuid "e224aaed-7ace-5ee6-9efa-77876f3b74e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-69$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517373} {:answer/id #uuid "e2822869-04a9-5b0d-8a9d-94e5390e105e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$189$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b20f23c0-8c87-5d2b-ba53-496addf07a38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$69$ cars per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517356} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c87e9ae-3f6c-51f1-aa5d-040dc2bf3415" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517338}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f2e135c6-4cc0-5a93-bc48-e0df9714cad2" :question/problem "A factory begins work at $8\\text{:}00$ am. Its order rate is $O(t)=100t e^{-0.1t}$ cars per hour and its completion rate is $C(t)=40+20\\sin(2\\pi t/6)$ cars per hour, where $t$ is hours after work begins. What is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction at the 24-hour time $9\\text{:}30$? Orders enter construction immediately. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change is the order rate minus the completion rate. The elapsed time is $t=(570-480)/60=1.5$ hours.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(1.5)-C(1.5) & =100(1.5){e}^{-0.1(1.5)}-(40+20\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{6}(1.5))) \\\\  & =100(1.5){e}^{-0.15}-40-20\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\\\  & =100(1.5){e}^{-0.15}-60 \\\\  & \\approx 69.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $69$ cars per hour."}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129147 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128963 :question/id #uuid "e158501f-0bac-5d16-956a-59da7f82620f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5818" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7dc5d6aa3a8afed8ebcf49b6d884eee8a443bc759367b624bc7a92cfae515863.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y = (x+2)(x+1)^2(x-2)?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=\\pm 2$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at these points. Moreover, because $x=\\pm 2$ are simple roots, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at these points.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=-1$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at this point.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\textbf{I}$  and $\\textbf{III}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is positive, as $x$  approaches $\\infty,$ $y$  approaches  $\\infty.$\n\nOnly graph $\\textbf{III}$ displays this end behavior. Therefore, the correct answer is **$\\textbf{III}$**."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d03ac24f-82a6-5af8-b1b8-9021e521d47a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129681 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cc95e90-e6ba-525f-a83f-104d53e7c3a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324331} {:answer/id #uuid "575c25ea-3c8f-5214-a7ba-34592633f0a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324696} {:answer/id #uuid "5f507194-bc49-50c1-be1b-2724a39b00c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324766} {:answer/id #uuid "d034069a-e837-5cba-8556-7b461bd05448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{III}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325782} {:answer/id #uuid "e393b641-9e73-5ed2-a4cd-a1bc68a62b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e393b641-9e73-5ed2-a4cd-a1bc68a62b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325972} :answer-field/id #uuid "030f2d36-3a47-5621-9486-f697bb4d38f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326225}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0deda6d-d55e-5ff9-9b25-84b2554afbce" :question/math-academy-id "q-38630" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8f21144219a628cbaf96d7ca052e14dd2e619c4776d49208cdd42305fc51180b.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=x(x+1)(x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=0,\\pm 1$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at these points. Moreover, because $x=0,\\pm 1$ are simple roots, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at these points.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{II}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is positive, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $\\infty .$ Since only graph $\\text{IV}$ displays this end behavior, the correct answer is $\\text{IV}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d3fe6cf-250a-5e20-8d08-3aa40ca54cf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{III}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325170} {:answer/id #uuid "b8090288-ea67-5ddf-a31d-10e0bdc7bc4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325550} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0f5a08-2bb5-5901-908c-752ab4fb9db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325740} {:answer/id #uuid "eddcaa70-0657-5597-81d6-f208d4caaf80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326062} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d5654b-2ff8-56f0-aa76-e5eb1572e943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8090288-ea67-5ddf-a31d-10e0bdc7bc4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325550} :answer-field/id #uuid "afa83f1c-5dfc-58f6-a447-8627519abfa7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326537}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a258d53-768b-53db-ad8c-9114ea48f386" :question/math-academy-id "q-38632" :question/problem "![](images/10/10af2af004ec61307d14a56f61a4a14acc87ded9ed38c3168c6b165b412eb5f0.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=-5{x}^{2}(x-1{)}^{2}(x-2)?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=2$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=2$ is a simple root, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=0,1$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at these points.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{I}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is negative, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $-\\infty .$\n\nOnly graph $\\text{IV}$ displays this end behavior. Therefore, the correct answer is $\\text{IV}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dc60b75-554d-58d0-b027-ef3b794160a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{III}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245720} {:answer/id #uuid "c7100d83-8d57-52e6-94e1-b855e81e9f6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246077} {:answer/id #uuid "ce812ba4-0a43-5778-955c-7bd1edb83e74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246159} {:answer/id #uuid "dbae5fd7-431f-5c98-a632-966ebf920961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246265} {:answer/id #uuid "e210e43b-42d1-5c93-91f6-fb894fd6ce1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7100d83-8d57-52e6-94e1-b855e81e9f6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246077} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2ce298d-c1f9-5147-8aa9-67f9aa805a1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246873}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e82163b8-d12f-5c46-89d0-bd29c13ba90d" :question/math-academy-id "q-112599" :question/problem "![](images/15/1586e286d2b07aac28a42f91c76318ae209c46c19e14e429c62f0770ada9393b.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=-x(x+2)^{2}(x-2)^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=-2$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=0$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross