/id #uuid "6d51d14a-53cb-5c26-a978-c14ba4c56bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518440} {:answer/id #uuid "e03dd380-944f-5a4c-9aa3-abe3deec68dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518465} {:answer/id #uuid "f535f8c7-10b4-5067-85e1-e6fe8f1d391e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518470} {:answer/id #uuid "fb2df4f9-9f00-597e-8895-7f08521446dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f535f8c7-10b4-5067-85e1-e6fe8f1d391e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518470} :answer-field/id #uuid "87f02f1d-859e-5c8d-827f-e07649812779" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518446}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "688c3a50-32ad-5270-8414-4ef95a767bb1" :question/problem "![](images/20/2058e3c4ae87ff2eb7fa1edcfdbb1ddb738217f771a7a41a7d2a234357f4a1d7.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=-(x-3)(x-2)^{2}(x-4)^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=2$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=3$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=3$ is a simple root, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=4$ is $3,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=4$ is a triple-root, the graph must be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{I}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is negative, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $-\\infty .$ Since only graph $\\text{I}$ displays this end behavior, the correct answer is $\\text{I}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518445 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09c9ab40-d5a1-558f-84a4-fd5cf8d2c443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{III}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518418} {:answer/id #uuid "4a52eef1-e553-5c29-94c0-112534b93570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518427} {:answer/id #uuid "5620b621-d406-5b4f-be64-03043c162940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518431} {:answer/id #uuid "9146bbeb-8444-5dcc-ab5a-bad6cff6e35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518448} {:answer/id #uuid "ffe8001d-ec1a-50c2-9954-9ab8b9817947" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9146bbeb-8444-5dcc-ab5a-bad6cff6e35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518448} :answer-field/id #uuid "76120e54-f08c-5654-95b1-6e5eb361e975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518441}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "803ed13b-598e-53ca-be59-31ca527c5ff3" :question/problem "![](images/ef/efb65216ce1440f34c5c0fbbc8a29b263b06556cc1858084db8e4549ec4e50e6.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=(x-1)(x-4)?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about t