e original equation has the solutions $x=1,2,$ and their product is $1\\cdot 2=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1028be-8d0a-5188-a153-5c206606fdcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e1028be-8d0a-5188-a153-5c206606fdcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518322} :answer-field/id #uuid "677ae855-f9cd-570b-8ead-84bf152f5f09" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518326} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079d95e9-b531-50ab-8f22-ed3dd2e2f2fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "079d95e9-b531-50ab-8f22-ed3dd2e2f2fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518319} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5b12cb7-30db-51fa-8b1c-a368a245bb18" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518343}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "687c8f09-08ba-5f3e-a91b-2c278344272b" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $12{x}^{2}\\cdot {8}^{x-3}+7x\\cdot {8}^{x-3}-49\\cdot {8}^{x-3}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{2}\\cdot {8}^{x-3}+7x\\cdot {8}^{x-3}-49\\cdot {8}^{x-3} & =0 \\\\ (12{x}^{2}+7x-49){8}^{x-3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n12{x}^{2}+7x-49=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{8}^{x-3}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $12{x}^{2}+7x-49=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(4x-7)(3x+7)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{7}{3},\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\n- The equation ${8}^{x-3}=0$ has no solutions because ${8}^{x-3}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{7}{3}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=\\frac{7}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "305eb9ca-2b6f-5e3b-8b2a-f2cde63da31f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518323} {:answer/id #uuid "8c2b9386-067f-51c1-8298-874a506a15a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{19}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518328} {:answer/id #uuid "9e412787-ad1d-51d9-ab5e-2f52dc4625fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518329} {:answer/id #uuid "be3c51c6-1895-5c6a-9cb8-273ea3fe5a09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518335} {:answer/id #uuid "e90f0201-bb0f-5f53-afbb-62e3940a0fce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e412787-ad1d-51d9-ab5e-2f52dc4625fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518329} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac740952-38ab-52bb-a6f2-4d6f9ae137ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518331}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ae55bf0c-c4b6-5b6c-a289-5c5d946d9710" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation $6{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1}+19x\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1}+15\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1}+19x\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1}+15\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1} & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}+19x+15){4}^{-3x+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+19x+15=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{4}^{-3x+1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $6{x}^{2}+19x+15=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x+5)(2x+3)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{5}{3},-\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n- The equation ${4}^{-3x+1}=0$ has no solutions because ${4}^{-3x+1}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-\\frac{5}{3},-\\frac{3}{2},$ and their product is $-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot -\\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518333 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c78e95da-59d8-5614-bc41-9acf11659f0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c78e95da-59d8-5614-bc41-9acf11659f0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518337} :answer-field/id #uuid "00de4d7f-a1f4-52d2-8929-7339b84f20bf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518318} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7b9c63b-25e3-58a8-acb7-7a5e354fcba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7b9c63b-25e3-58a8-acb7-7a5e354fcba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518338} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9bf8df2-6ab5-5be6-b2b0-d25230d29452" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518340}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0e3548f-1fa8-5d7e-a0b1-0803e5136f3c" :question/problem "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $8{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2}+34x\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2}+21\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2}+34x\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2}+21\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2} & =0 \\\\ (8{x}^{2}+34x+21){7}^{-2x-2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n8{x}^{2}+34x+21=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{7}^{-2x-2}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $8{x}^{2}+34x+21=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(4x+3)(2x+7)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\n- The equation ${7}^{-2x-2}=0$ has no solutions because ${7}^{-2x-2}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{7}{2}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa5c0758-ea4e-559c-9fa6-6da92f3f864c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa5c0758-ea4e-559c-9fa6-6da92f3f864c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518344} :answer-field/id #uuid "08eda422-e04b-5930-81c5-41c5a7d27c16" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0f7c0ad-acc2-55a6-9ee0-58a4368e20e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0f7c0ad-acc2-55a6-9ee0-58a4368e20e0" :answer/type {:db/iden